WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.000
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.133
You're here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.000
You made it.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.734
Thank you for watching.
Thanks for being here.

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.000
Well, guys,
this is very exciting.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.267
Tomorrow is
the official start of summer.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:16.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Tomorrow.

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:19.000
I love summer,
although I could have done

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.200
without this on my subway ride
to work today.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.667
A guy handed me sunscreen and
asked if I would do his back.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.934
I go --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:27.601
Here's some good news.
Starting tomorrow,

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:32.234
COVID vaccine shots will be
available to kids 5 and under.

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:35.567
Yeah, that's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:37.901
That's -- That's right, kiddos.
No more excuses.

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.100
Time to head back to the office
like the rest of us.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.701
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:44.601
Yep, kids can finally get
vaccinated against COVID.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.033
Meanwhile,
Chuck E. Cheese was like,

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.234
[ Puffs cigarette ] "I still
wouldn't touch that ball pit."

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:52.033
[ Coughing ]
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.033
That's right.
Kids as young as 6 months

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:57.133
can get Pfizer's
three-dose vaccine.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:59.167
Yep, every parents dream --
taking their kid

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:00.968
three times in a row
to get a shot.

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:03.000
[ Laughter ]
Three shots.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.300
Right now, parents are like,
"What the hell?

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.834
Might as well
get their ears pierced, too."

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:07.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.400
Well, everyone's
been talking about this.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.734
Over the weekend,
President Biden

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:12.467
was on a bike ride...

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:16.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:20.434
I don't even need to do a joke.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:23.334
-He's going for a bike ride
near his beach house in Delaware

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:24.567
when he took a little spill.

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.667
Here, check this out,
if you haven't seen it.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.801
[ Cheers ]

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:40.400
[ Sad tuba ]

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.901
[ Laughter ]
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:47.067
Poor Biden.
Even his bike was like,

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:49.000
"I'm sorry, but I can
no longer support you."

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:54.868
If you want to see
that clip again,

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:57.367
it's airing on a 24-hour loop
on Fox News.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:02.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:05.200
Yeah, it's --
it's shocking.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.167
Not the fall, that Biden looks
kind of good in bike shorts.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.834
That's what I thought.
I go, "Interesting."

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.234
That's right, Biden fell
and everyone has jokes,

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:15.000
but no one ever talks about how
good he used to be on a bike.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.501
Do you guys remember this video?

00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:17.701
♪♪

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:18.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:19.934
They never show that.

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.000
I mean, that was back --
that was back before --

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.100
-Wow!
-That was back before

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.734
you had toe clips or whatever.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.734 --> 00:02:26.234
[ Laughter ]
Penny-farthing.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:27.634
-Yeah.
Speaking of the President,

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:30.801
according to a recent poll,
most Americans do not want Biden

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:34.834
or former President Trump
to run again in 2024.

00:02:34.834 --> 00:02:37.267
Yeah, in two years, America is
gonna walk into a voting booth

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:39.501
like, "Uh, can we choose
'None of the above'?

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:41.601
What are we --"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:44.100
I think we're at the point now
where 2024 is just gonna be

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.501
holograms of JFK and Reagan.
You go...

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:48.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.701
It's a tough choice.
People are like,

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:51.234
"Do I want a guy
who can't ride a bike

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:52.701
or a guy who can't
walk down a ramp?

00:02:52.701 --> 00:03:02.334
I don't know which --"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:05.267
Well, on Saturday,
Trump held a rally in Memphis,

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:07.334
and he said pretty much
what you'd expect.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:08.934
So, instead of showing
the same clips

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:10.334
you've seen a million times,
it's time

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:12.367
for another installment of
"Trump With No Context."

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:13.434
Enjoy.

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:16.601
♪♪

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:19.767
Shyeah!
Ahhh!

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.534
[ Grunts ]

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.534
Unnhhh!

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:25.567
Unh!

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.367
♪♪

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:32.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:36.334
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:38.901
-You guys see this?
Apparently, HBO is working on

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:42.934
a "Game of Thrones" spinoff
series based around Jon Snow.

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:46.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.467
I'm pretty sure
that already exists.

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:49.334
It's called "Game of Thrones."
Am I wrong?

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:52.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.434
That would be like NBC
creating a "Seinfeld" spinoff

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.634
based on Jerry.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.834
Hey, this is exciting.
A new trailer for the next

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:02.234
"Fast &amp; Furious" sequel
just came out,

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:04.667
and I gotta say,
it looks pretty intense.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:05.701
Check this out.

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:06.767
[ Engines revving ]

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:10.000
-This summer,
fasten your seatbelts

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.334
because the family
is getting back together

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:18.033
for one more epic ride.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.801
"Fast &amp; Furious X:
Joe-Kyo Drift."

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:25.868
[ Bike bell rings ]

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:28.000
Presented in partnership
with Metamucil.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.701
-"Joe-Kyo Drift."
-"Joe-Kyo."

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:34.234
-[ Laughs ]
"Joe-Kyo Drift."

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:35.534
Yeah.
-"Joe-Kyo Drift."

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:36.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:39.300
Wow.
-Hey, guys, get this.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.667
I heard about a guy
who was addicted to Pepsi

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:44.667
and said he drank
30 cans a day for 20 years.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:45.868
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.501
Yeah, asked what
finally made him stop, he said,

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:51.601
"I tried a Coke."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:54.701
Yeah, he's totally fine, except
if you shake him, he explodes.

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:56.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:59.067
Ladies and gentlemen, I read
that, according to a new poll,

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:02.734
Americans only feel relaxed
for about 40 minutes a day.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:03.834
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:06.100
I thought we'd try
to get that up to 41

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.167
by sharing some
relaxing thoughts, right now,

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:09.934
during this show.
Can I get some music, please?

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:11.000
[ Soft music plays ]
[ Clears throat ]

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.534
Here we go.

00:05:12.534 --> 00:05:16.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:17.934
Hey.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:22.300
No one remembers
that you had bangs.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:28.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.501
When your friends
make a new group chat,

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:32.334
they type in your name first.

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:35.801
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:41.801
Every day, your mailman's like,
"Oh, my God.

00:05:41.801 --> 00:05:43.267
This is the most mail
I've ever seen!"

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:47.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:49.901
You're not a wimp for peeling
off the pudding skin.

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:51.100
That stuff's gross.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:54.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:54.467 --> 00:05:57.701
If he met you, Channing Tatum
would probably like you.

00:05:57.701 --> 00:06:03.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:07.234
That e-mail that you've been
meaning to send for two years,

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:10.100
when you finally send it,
it'll be that much more special.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:14.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.901
Last night at dinner,
you said something so funny,

00:06:16.901 --> 00:06:18.734
the waiter
told the chef about it.

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:22.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:25.234
♪♪

00:06:25.234 --> 00:06:26.501
Nobody flosses.

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:31.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:31.601 --> 00:06:34.100
Everyone's knees crack a little
when they kneel.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.100
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:38.634
The cooler you are,
the louder they crunch.

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:43.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:46.467
And finally, you look great
in that first selfie.

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:47.901
There's no need
to take any more.

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:49.200
[ Laughter ]
You nailed it.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.334 --> 00:06:51.968
Thank you.
I feel better.

00:06:51.968 --> 00:06:54.367
I feel better.
I feel more relaxed.

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:57.000
I feel better.
Thank you.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.701
[ Applause ]

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:01.367
Well, it was a crazy travel
weekend all over the world.

00:07:01.367 --> 00:07:03.534
And I saw that there was
a luggage malfunction

00:07:03.534 --> 00:07:07.100
at the London Heathrow Airport
that created a bit of a backup.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.267
If you haven't seen this,
take a look at this.

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:22.200
-Oh!
-Wow.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:24.033
-It's odd when an airline
loses your baggage

00:07:24.033 --> 00:07:25.868
but also knows
exactly where it is.

00:07:25.868 --> 00:07:27.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.000
One woman said,
"That's why I tie

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.300
a little red ribbon on my bag."

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:34.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.467
Meanwhile, T.J.Maxx is like,
"Looks fine to us.

00:07:36.467 --> 00:07:37.767
That looks cool.
That's normal."

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:39.033
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:41.033
And finally, it's time
for our latest installment

00:07:41.033 --> 00:07:42.200
of "Tonight Show" Polls.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:43.634
Here we go,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:07:43.634 --> 00:07:48.367
-♪ "Tonight Show Polls" ♪

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.200
Now this first poll asked...

00:08:02.567 --> 00:08:05.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:07.267 --> 00:08:08.634
This next poll asked...

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.300
And there you go. Alright.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:23.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:26.634
No. We're good.

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:28.067
This next poll asked...

00:08:41.501 --> 00:08:45.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.734
This next poll said...

00:08:53.467 --> 00:08:56.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:58.767 --> 00:09:00.968
"I'm a genius."

00:09:00.968 --> 00:09:02.033
This next one asked...

00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:16.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:16.667 --> 00:09:17.934
This last poll asked...

00:09:29.834 --> 00:09:31.968
That's all the time we have
for "Tonight Show Polls."

